#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:8
msgid ""
"A pouch cell stack resolved through its thickness. The stack's "
"`num_physical_layers` unit cells are lumped into `num_subdivisions` zones, "
"and each zone is PyBaMM's own model for its unit cells in parallel: `pybamm."
"lithium_ion.SPM` (`MultiLayer3DThermalSPM`), `SPMe` "
"(`MultiLayer3DThermalSPMe`), or `DFN` (`MultiLayer3DThermalDFN`), built with "
"the options the stack is given. Particle phases, open-circuit potential "
"models (hysteresis included), intercalation kinetics, and every other "
"electrochemical option therefore behave exactly as they do in that model. "
"Every zone also carries its own temperature field `T_i(x, y, z)` on a 3D "
"finite-element mesh, which replaces the zone model's lumped temperature: the "
"field's source is the zone's total heating, and its volume average is the "
"temperature the zone's kinetics and transport see. Adjacent zones exchange "
"heat by conduction through the stack plus a contact resistance, and every "
"exposed face is cooled convectively. The zones connect in parallel, each "
"with its current solved for, or in series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:24
msgid ""
"Prefer it to `pybamm.lithium_ion.Basic3DThermalSPM` when the question is "
"about the stack's thickness: a cooling plate on one face, a degraded layer, "
"anything that makes the layers of a pouch run at different temperatures. "
"That model has one temperature field and one electrochemistry for the whole "
"cell, so it cannot move current between layers. Prefer PyBaMM's `\"lumped\"` "
"or `\"x-full\"` thermal options when the stack is close to isothermal "
"through its thickness; they are far cheaper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:32
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:34
msgid ""
"Each zone's 3D mesh needs PyBaMM's finite-element extra, which the model's "
"extra installs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:37
msgid "pip install \"pybamm-model-zoo[zoo-multilayer-3d-thermal]\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:41
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"\n"
"model = zoo.load(\"MultiLayer3DThermalSPM\")(num_physical_layers=24, "
"num_subdivisions=6)\n"
"parameter_values = model.apply_stack_scaling(model."
"default_parameter_values)\n"
"parameter_values.update(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"Left face heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 50.0,\n"
"        model.CONTACT_RESISTANCE_PARAM: 1e-2,\n"
"    }\n"
")\n"
"simulation = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model,\n"
"    parameter_values=parameter_values,\n"
"    experiment=pybamm.Experiment([\"Discharge at 3C until 2.8 V\"]),\n"
")\n"
"solution = simulation.solve()\n"
"print(solution[\"Temperature spread [K]\"](solution.t[-1]))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:62
msgid "The SPMe and DFN variants take the same arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:64
msgid ""
"from pybamm_model_zoo.multilayer_3d_thermal import (\n"
"    MultiLayer3DThermalDFN,\n"
"    MultiLayer3DThermalSPMe,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:71
msgid ""
"`examples/run_multilayer_3d_thermal.py` cools a stack through one face and "
"follows the current as it moves to the warm side and back. `examples/"
"compare_electrochemistry.py` runs the same stack with all three "
"electrochemistries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:76
msgid "Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:78
msgid "`num_physical_layers` — unit cells in the stack, at least 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:79
msgid ""
"`num_subdivisions` — zones, at least 2 and a divisor of "
"`num_physical_layers`; defaults to one zone per unit cell. Fewer zones are "
"cheaper, and under uniform cooling give the same answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:82
msgid ""
"`connection` — `\"parallel\"` or `\"series\"`. The unit cells within a zone "
"are always in parallel. In series, the stack stops when any one zone reaches "
"the parameter set's voltage cut-offs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:85
msgid ""
"`mesh_h` — target element size of each zone's mesh, as for `pybamm."
"ScikitFemGenerator3D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:87
msgid ""
"`options` — model options, given to every zone. `\"thermal\"` must be "
"`\"lumped\"`, `\"dimensionality\"` 0, and `\"cell geometry\"` `\"pouch\"`: "
"the stack's fields are the thermal model, and each zone keeps a lumped "
"temperature for them to replace. `\"surface temperature\"` is recorded on "
"the stack's `options` only, since the zones have no casing; the stack "
"reports its own face temperatures either way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:93
msgid ""
"`zone_model` — `zone_model(options)` returning one zone's built model, in "
"place of `ZONE_MODEL(options=options)`: for example a model built with "
"`build=False` whose thermal submodel is replaced before it is built. It must "
"honour the options it is handed and keep a lumped temperature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:97
msgid ""
"`coating` — `\"double-sided\"` (default) or `\"single-sided\"`: whether "
"neighbouring unit cells share their current collector foils. See \"Unit "
"cells and foils\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:100
msgid ""
"For example, a silicon-graphite negative electrode with hysteresis on the "
"silicon and Marcus-Hush-Chidsey kinetics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:103
msgid ""
"model = MultiLayer3DThermalSPMe(\n"
"    num_physical_layers=24,\n"
"    num_subdivisions=4,\n"
"    options={\n"
"        \"particle phases\": (\"2\", \"1\"),\n"
"        \"open-circuit potential\": ((\"single\", \"one-state hysteresis\"), "
"\"single\"),\n"
"        \"intercalation kinetics\": (\"Marcus-Hush-Chidsey\", \"symmetric "
"Butler-Volmer\"),\n"
"    },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:115
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:117
msgid ""
"The parameter set describes one unit cell, and `\"Current function [A]\"` is "
"the current through the whole stack. `apply_stack_scaling` multiplies "
"`\"Nominal cell capacity [A.h]\"` by the unit cells that share that current "
"— all of them in parallel, one zone's in series — so that an experiment's C-"
"rate is each unit cell's own. Leave `\"Number of electrodes connected in "
"parallel to make a cell\"` at 1: the stack's unit cells are this model's "
"layers, and setting it too would divide the current twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:125
msgid "Unit cells and foils"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:127
msgid ""
"`\"Negative current collector thickness [m]\"` and `\"Positive current "
"collector thickness [m]\"` are always the thickness of a whole foil, as in "
"PyBaMM's own parameter sets, whatever the coating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:131
msgid ""
"With `coating=\"double-sided\"`, the default, each foil is coated on both "
"faces and serves the unit cells on either side of it, so the stack "
"alternates direction and every unit cell owns half of each foil:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:135
msgid ""
"          unit cell k                unit cell k+1\n"
"   |<------------------------->|<------------------------->|\n"
"   ½Cu |  n  |  s  |  p  | ½Al ½Al |  p  |  s  |  n  | ½Cu ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:141
msgid ""
"One unit cell is then `L_n + L_s + L_p + (L_cc,n + L_cc,p) / 2` thick "
"(`unit_cell_thickness`), and the stack `num_physical_layers` times that. "
"With `coating=\"single-sided\"`, every unit cell has whole foils of its own, "
"as PyBaMM's single-cell models assume, and is `L_n + L_s + L_p + L_cc,n + "
"L_cc,p` thick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:146
msgid ""
"Double-sided is the default because it is how stacked pouch cells are built: "
"every inner electrode is coated on both faces of its foil. Counting a whole "
"foil per unit cell would make such a stack too thick, give it too much foil "
"mass and heat capacity, and overstate its in-plane conductivity, by a share "
"that grows with the foils' fraction of the unit cell (12% of the thickness "
"for 6 µm copper and 15 µm aluminium foils under 80 µm of electrodes and "
"separator). Single-sided is kept for cells whose electrodes are coated on "
"one face only, and to compare with PyBaMM's single-cell models, which carry "
"whole foils, under the same parameter set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:156
msgid ""
"A unit cell's foil share enters everything that depends on the foils' "
"thickness: the stack's thickness, so the volume each zone's heat is spread "
"over; the thickness-weighted heat capacity and in-plane thermal "
"conductivity; and the series conduction through the stack. With `\"use "
"lumped thermal capacity\"`, `\"Cell heat capacity [J.K-1.m-3]\"` is per "
"volume of this unit cell. The electrochemistry does not depend on the foils' "
"thickness. The two outermost foils serve a single unit cell, so a double-"
"sided stack is half a foil short at each outer face."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:165
msgid ""
"`default_parameter_values` and `apply_stack_scaling` add these where the "
"parameter set lacks them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:168
msgid ""
"`\"Inter-layer thermal contact resistance [K.m2.W-1]\"`, default `0`: "
"contact resistance between adjacent zones, an adhesive or gas gap, on top of "
"conduction through the zones themselves. Each zone's field conducts with "
"`lambda_eff`, the in-plane mean, so the interface between two zones carries "
"their series conduction, `zone_series_resistance(T)`: the unit cell's "
"layers, each foil at the unit cell's share of it, as thermal resistances in "
"series, times the unit cells in a zone. The two outer zones carry half a "
"zone of it in series with the cooling of the stack's outer faces. The "
"layers' thicknesses and thermal conductivities therefore set the through-"
"stack conductivity, and the number of unit cells the stack's thickness: a "
"stack of thicker electrodes, or more of them, holds a larger core-to-skin "
"difference. The metal foils are a negligible part of it (0.06% on "
"`Marquis2019` with whole foils)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:180
msgid ""
"`\"<Face> face heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\"` for the `Left` (`x = "
"0`, zone 0's outer face), `Right`, `Front`, `Back`, `Bottom`, and `Top` "
"faces, default `10`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:184
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:186
msgid "Per zone `i`, each prefixed `\"Layer i \"`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:188
msgid "`temperature [K]` — the 3D field — and `average temperature [K]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:189
msgid ""
"`heat generation [W.m-3]` and `heat capacity [J.K-1.m-3]`, per unit volume "
"of a unit cell, current collectors included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:191
msgid ""
"`voltage [V]`, `current [A]` (the zone's), `per-unit-cell current [A]`, and, "
"in parallel, `current fraction`, which is undefined at rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:193
msgid ""
"`Total current density [A.m-2]`, PyBaMM's per-unit-cell current density, and "
"each electrode's `X-averaged ... interfacial current density [A.m-2]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:195
msgid ""
"A selection of the zone model's own variables under their PyBaMM names, for "
"one unit cell: the `X-averaged ` and `Volume-averaged ` concentrations, "
"stoichiometries, open-circuit potentials, hysteresis states, overpotentials, "
"ohmic losses and heat terms; `Surface open-circuit voltage [V]`, `Discharge "
"capacity [A.h]`, `Total lithium in electrolyte [mol]`, the heat terms in "
"watts (`Total heating [W]`, `Reversible heating [W]`, ...), and, where the "
"model has them, the electrolyte concentration and potential and the "
"electrode potentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:204
msgid ""
"For the stack: `Voltage [V]`, `Current [A]`, `Total current density [A.m-2]` "
"(the mean over its unit cells), `Volume-averaged total heating [W.m-3]`, the "
"heat terms in watts and `Discharge capacity [A.h]` summed over every unit "
"cell, and its temperatures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:209
msgid ""
"`Left face temperature [K]` and `Right face temperature [K]` — the stack's "
"two outer faces (zone 0's `x_min` and the last zone's `x_max`), each "
"averaged over the footprint and named as its heat transfer coefficient is, "
"so that under one-sided cooling it is clear which face is which."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:213
msgid ""
"`Surface temperature [K]` — the mean of the two outer faces, where a skin "
"thermocouple sits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:215
msgid ""
"`Core temperature [K]` — the stack's mid-plane, averaged over the footprint: "
"the mean of the two faces at the middle interface for an even number of "
"zones, the middle zone's average for an odd number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:218
msgid "`Core-to-skin temperature difference [K]` — core minus surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:219
msgid ""
"`Stack-averaged temperature [K]` — the volume average (also as `Volume-"
"averaged cell temperature [K]` and `X-averaged cell temperature [K]`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:221
msgid ""
"`Maximum layer-averaged temperature [K]`, `Minimum layer-averaged "
"temperature [K]`, and `Temperature spread [K]`, their difference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:224
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:226
msgid ""
"All of these run in `tests/test_multilayer_3d_thermal.py`, with "
"`Marquis2019` unless stated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:229
msgid ""
"Held isothermal by cooling every face at `1e4 W.m-2.K-1`, a symmetric two-"
"zone stack matches `pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM`, `SPMe`, and `DFN` to within 1 "
"mV over a 30 minute discharge (measured 0.013, 0.008, and 0.005 mV)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:232
msgid ""
"With a two-phase negative electrode and one-state hysteresis on its "
"secondary phase (`Chen2020_composite`), with Butler-Volmer or Marcus-Hush-"
"Chidsey kinetics on the negative electrode, the SPM, SPMe and DFN stacks "
"match PyBaMM's own models under the same options to within 1 mV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:236
msgid ""
"PyBaMM's own `\"heat of mixing\"`, where it builds (one particle phase), "
"reaches every zone, and an insulated stack heats as a lumped cell with the "
"same option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:238
msgid ""
"With `\"use lumped thermal capacity\"`, each zone's heat capacity is `\"Cell "
"heat capacity [J.K-1.m-3]\"`, and an insulated stack heats as a lumped cell "
"with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:240
msgid ""
"`\"surface temperature\": \"lumped\"` is kept on the stack's options, and "
"the zones stay without a casing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:242
msgid ""
"A `zone_model` that swaps a submodel before building gives the same solution "
"when the swapped-in submodel is PyBaMM's own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:244
msgid ""
"An experiment discharges to its own voltage cut-off, below the parameter "
"set's, in parallel and in series: no zone keeps a voltage limit the "
"experiment does not relax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:247
msgid ""
"In series, cooled through one face, the cold zone reaching the lower or "
"upper cut-off stops the stack, with the warm zone still inside its limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:249
msgid ""
"Insulated on every face, the stack heats as PyBaMM's lumped model of one "
"unit cell to `rtol=1e-3` (measured 1e-5 and better): the same heat, over the "
"same volume, current collectors included, and the same heat capacity. A "
"double-sided stack matches a lumped cell given half of each foil; a single-"
"sided one, a lumped cell with whole foils."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:254
msgid ""
"A unit cell is its electrodes and separator plus half of each foil when "
"double-sided, or whole foils when single-sided, in the stack's geometry and "
"in its series conduction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:257
msgid ""
"Insulated on every face, the stack stores the heat it generates to within "
"0.1% (measured 0.002%). This pins the interface coupling: heat leaves one "
"zone exactly as it enters the next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:260
msgid ""
"The stack's heat terms in watts are its zones' times the unit cells in each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:261
msgid "The SPMe and DFN electrolytes conserve lithium to `rtol=1e-9`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:262
msgid ""
"A uniform parallel stack starts from rest with no current in any zone, then "
"shares the load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:264
msgid ""
"After a discharge cooled through one face, the zones balance at rest: the "
"cold zone, which carried less of the discharge, gives current to the warm "
"one, and the zone currents sum to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:267
msgid ""
"PyBaMM's `\"contact resistance\"` option drops each unit cell's voltage by "
"its own current times `\"Contact resistance [Ohm]\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:269
msgid ""
"Cooled through both big faces, core-to-skin is the same in 2 zones as in 12, "
"and within 5% of a uniformly heated slab conducting in series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:271
msgid ""
"Cooled alike on both big faces, with odd and even numbers of zones, the two "
"face temperatures agree, the surface sits below the stack average and the "
"core above it. Cooled on the left face only, the left face is the colder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:274
msgid ""
"The interface resistance is the unit cell's layers in series, far below the "
"in-plane `lambda_eff`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:276
msgid ""
"A symmetric two-zone parallel stack splits its current evenly, with no "
"temperature spread, for all three electrochemistries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:278
msgid ""
"Cooled through one face, the zones warm monotonically away from it, and two "
"thirds of the way through a 2C discharge the warmer zones carry "
"monotonically more of the current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:281
msgid ""
"Six unit cells in two zones reproduce six in six under uniform cooling: the "
"voltage to 10 µV and the stack temperature to 1 mK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:283
msgid ""
"After `apply_stack_scaling`, 1C drives every unit cell at the parameter "
"set's own 1C current, in parallel and in series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:286
msgid "Not validated, and worth knowing before relying on it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:288
msgid ""
"Nothing has been compared with an experiment or a published multilayer model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:289
msgid ""
"Inside a zone the field conducts with `lambda_eff`, the in-plane mean, in "
"every direction, so a zone is close to isothermal through its own thickness; "
"the series conduction through the stack sits on the interfaces between zone "
"centres and at the outer faces. More zones resolve the shape of the profile "
"and a non-uniform heat source, not its core-to-skin difference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:294
msgid ""
"A zone's electrochemistry sees only its own volume-averaged temperature, so "
"the field's in-plane gradients carry heat but do not feed back into the "
"kinetics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:296
msgid "Each zone generates its heat uniformly over its volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:297
msgid ""
"`\"heat of mixing\": \"true\"` is PyBaMM's own term, which does not build on "
"an electrode with more than one particle phase; a zone model with its own "
"thermal submodel can be passed as `zone_model` until it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:300
msgid ""
"Tabs, current collector resistance beyond PyBaMM's `\"contact resistance\"` "
"option, and in-plane current distribution within a layer are not modelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:303
msgid "Citation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:305
msgid ""
"See `CITATION.bib`. Cite `MultiLayer3DThermal2026` for this entry, and "
"`Marquis2019` for the SPM and SPMe zones or `Doyle1993` for the DFN zones. "
"Each is registered when the model is instantiated, so `pybamm."
"print_citations()` lists them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/multilayer_3d_thermal/README.md:310
msgid "Maintainer"
msgstr ""

